                <pb facs="0779" n="767" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg767"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/18525: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-01-21T17:00:00-05:00">January 21, 1942—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>169. Your 139, January 14, 5 p.m. With respect to the second paragraph of your
                    telegram, as you are aware, the Department’s position continues to be based upon
                    the military (not commercial) nature of Lati and its service.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
